    "abstract": "Parts figure for the aft hold smoke detection installation, showing the sampling ports in their open and shielded standards, the detection regulator and the ceiling rail attachment hardware.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure shows the aft cargo compartment smoke detection installation: the two sampling ports, the sampling tube run and the detection regulator in the ceiling void.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the ceiling rail with the two sampling positions looking forward. Items 20 and 20A are the shielded inlet and the open port; they occupy different positions on the rail and the shielded inlet at item 20 must be used with the relocated tube run shown on sheet 2. The effectivity on these two items was reversed against the task text until this issue: the shielded inlet is the POST MOD-168024 item and the open port the PRE MOD-168024 item, and an order raised from the earlier issue of this figure will have brought the wrong one. The detection regulator at item 10 is common to both standards. Fastener quantity at item 40 is per port, not per aircraft."
    },
